From 01a1884b17b20b28dd85d11b42ec552f6af68d01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:03:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] icwmp: start-up trace + crash report (debug)

icwmpd died on the HP2236B board before 'STARTING ICWMP' with nothing in
the log: the pid-lock exit, the error returns of cwmp_init/main and the
ubus_connect failure are silent upstream, and a crash leaves no trace.

- icwmp_boot_trace(): every start step to stderr (procd -> logread) and
  /tmp/icwmpd_boot.log (append, capped 64 KiB), independent of cwmp.cpe.log_*
- SIGSEGV/SIGBUS/SIGILL/SIGFPE/SIGABRT handler: fault addr, pc/lr/sp,
  /proc/self/maps, then re-raise (core dump still possible)
- mtk init script: procd stdout 1 as well

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/config.c              |  24 ++-
 public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/cwmp.c                | 194 ++++++++++++++++++
 public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/inc/cwmp.h            |   4 +
 .../icwmp/icwmp/sdk/mtk/files/icwmpd.init     |   1 +
 public/apps/icwmp/icwmp/ubus.c                |  11 +-
 5 files changed, 231 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

